 ## Background
-Surface property estimation is a standard post-processing or pre-processing step in volume rendering pipelines. Normal estimation via finite differences is a classic technique in computer graphics [G]. Surface area estimation via triangle summation is a direct consequence of the polygonal approximation inherent in Marching Cubes [S1]. Smoothing binary embeddings to facilitate smoother isosurface extraction addresses the "stair-stepping" artifact common in discrete voxel data [S1].
+Surface property estimation is a standard step in computer graphics pipelines following mesh generation. Normal estimation is critical for shading, while area estimation is important for physical simulations and visualization. Smoothing techniques have evolved from simple post-processing filters to sophisticated field transformations to preserve detail in binary data [S1]. The specific iterative smoothing method for particle data was developed to handle large-scale SPH simulations [S1].
 
